**Le Morne** is the peninsula at the southwestern corner of Mauritius. It is dominated by the mountain of the same name and almost entirely surrounded by a lagoon.

## A place of memory

In the 18th and early 19th centuries people escaping slavery (known as maroons) found refuge in the caves and on the steep summit of Le Morne Brabant. According to oral tradition a police party climbed the mountain on 1 February 1835 to announce that slavery had been abolished. Those on the summit believed they were about to be recaptured and chose to leap to their deaths rather than return to slavery.

The story made the mountain a symbol of the fight for freedom and 1 February is commemorated in Mauritius as the day of the abolition of slavery. In 2008 the Le Morne Cultural Landscape was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List. The Slave Route Monument near the public beach honours those who sought refuge here.

## The beaches

Le Morne public beach on the west side of the peninsula has fine white sand and clear shallow water with the mountain rising behind it. Off the southwest tip sand and silt run off the edge of the reef into deep water. This creates the famous "underwater waterfall" illusion which you can only see from the air on a seaplane or helicopter flight.

## Kitesurfing

Le Morne is one of the best known kitesurfing spots in the world. There is flat water inside the lagoon for learning and on the outer reef a wave called One Eye for experts only. The trade winds are strongest and most reliable in the southern winter.

## Hiking Le Morne Brabant

A trail climbs the mountain from its eastern side. The lower part is an easy walk. The upper section is steep with some scrambling and access to it has been regulated at times. Check the current rules before you go and set off early to avoid the heat. Consider hiring a licensed local guide.

## Good to know

- Le Morne is a place of remembrance: treat the monument and the mountain with respect.
- The peninsula is roughly an hour and a quarter by car from the international airport.
